WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.630
- So wait, Nick, it took me,
I don't know how many minutes

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.360
my producer can tell me,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.300
it took me not long to
have a "Friends" reference

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.170
so I'm just saying, it was such a huge

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.090
pop culture impact on all of us.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.780
So, how many minutes into meeting David

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.130
did you actually ask a "Friends" question

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.530
or mention "Friends" at all?

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:22.320
- I don't know,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.011
I mean we haven't really spoken

00:00:24.011 --> 00:00:24.844
about it.
- Oh my gosh,

00:00:24.844 --> 00:00:26.250
don't you make me feel like an idiot!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.272
You didn't?

00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:28.479
- No, no, no, he-
(laughing)

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:31.112
- I was respecting David's
professional integrity

00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:32.531
but I think that-

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.000
- Professional integrity,
it was probably one of the

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.793
biggest shows ever on TV in life!

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.513
- I adore it.

00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:41.040
This thing was, I did have to,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.450
I mean David and I are mates now

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.900
but I guess in the first instance,

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.780
I obviously had to hold
my tongue a hell of a lot

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.420
because I grew up watching it.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.400
It's one of my favorite things ever

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.700
but I remember, actually I think David,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.990
you mentioned it first because I remember

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.930
we were doing an improv thing with Julia,

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.190
this was with Julia Davis

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.530
which was for a show that never happened

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.110
but David come over and we were doing some

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.600
improv stuff together

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.810
and I remember you in character said,

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.957
you left your phone with us
and you in character said,

00:01:10.957 --> 00:01:12.017
"I don't want you checking my phone.

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.180
"I've got Jennifer Aniston's
number on that phone."

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.970
And you said it in
character, and literally,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.078
me and Julia almost fell off our seats.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.258
(laughing)

00:01:20.258 --> 00:01:21.211
But other than that,

00:01:21.211 --> 00:01:23.469
I don't think we've really spoke about it.

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:25.530
Maybe there was one time
when I was gonna do,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.900
I was possibly considering
doing a play whilst-

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.800
- There was one story,
we had a meeting recently

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.100
or this year I think on breaking stories

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.140
for the second season
- Oh for season two, yeah.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.673
- which we're hopefully gonna
shoot this fall, we'll see,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.410
and Nick was talking about
pitching a story in which

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.457
my character got, what was it?

00:01:47.457 --> 00:01:50.057
- I think you got like
a fake tan or something

00:01:50.057 --> 00:01:52.710
and then you were like-
- Yeah, and I just said

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.600
yeah dude, we can't do that.
(laughing)

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.760
- But this is the thing,
this is the problem you know,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.550
it's such a successful show
with what, how many episodes?

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.295
250 or whatever it was.

00:02:02.295 --> 00:02:06.088
- 236, and I hope by now
you've seen them all, Nick.

00:02:06.088 --> 00:02:06.921
I mean...
- Oh course, yeah.

00:02:06.921 --> 00:02:09.416
- Apparently Nick isn't a fan but I am.

00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:10.249
(laughing)

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:11.510
- No I am a fan, I am a fan.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.480
But this is the thing,
it's such an iconic show

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.110
that you have to, when you're writing,

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.450
trying to like, break story
and do B plots and so on,

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.970
you suddenly realize
that "Friends" had done

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.860
pretty much everything.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.310
But I remember even,
there was a marketing idea

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.420
and I think I remember pitching it to,

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.050
not so much like, drinking
the stuff out of the straws,

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.097
the kind of, iconic "Friends" thing

00:02:30.097 --> 00:02:32.940
but I remember pitching
a marketing idea to you

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.773
and I think you said,

00:02:33.773 --> 00:02:35.170
"oh, we did it in "Friends,""
or something like that.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.632
- But we hadn't-
- I have a feeling

00:02:36.632 --> 00:02:37.882
you might say that a lot.

